title: 'pallet-psm: resolve admin roles from the internal asset owner'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A PSM admin role is an `AdminOrigin`: `AssetOwner` or `Origin(origin)`. `AssetOwner` is held by whoever owns the internal asset at the time of each admin call; `Origin(origin)` is held by that origin. `create_psm` takes an optional admin for each role, and `None` sets it to `AssetOwner`. `set_full_admin` and `set_emergency_admin` take an `AdminOrigin`. `PsmCreated`, `FullAdminChanged` and `EmergencyAdminChanged` carry `AdminOrigin`.

    `create_psm`, `set_full_admin` and `set_emergency_admin` use call indices 13, 14 and 15. Runtimes must add `pallet_psm::migrations::v1::MigrateV0ToV1`, which sets a stored role equal to the signed origin of the internal asset's current owner to `AssetOwner` and every other role to `Origin`, and must bump `transaction_version`.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    PSM admin calls by the signed owner of the internal asset succeed when the PSM's roles are `AssetOwner`. `create_psm`, `set_full_admin` and `set_emergency_admin` have new call indices and argument types.
crates:
- name: pallet-psm
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
